From e498a4c62301a9164b62c76fd3ded0e782282cb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:39:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/19] feat(core): pods_run takes command, args and
 restartPolicy; create-only unless replace (C7)

pods_run could only start an image's default entrypoint with restart
policy Always, so the tool meant for "run this in the cluster" could
not run a command: on the native session (job 7) the agent fell back to
a hand-written Pod manifest after six calls and two errors. A re-run
with the same name re-applied over the earlier Pod (the fixed build
already refuses objects pods_run did not create).

- `command` and `args` (arrays of strings) set the container's
  entrypoint and arguments; `restartPolicy` (Always, OnFailure, Never)
  allows one-off commands.
- A Pod, Service or Route that an earlier pods_run created under the
  same name is no longer re-applied silently: the call fails and says
  so. `replace: true` re-applies over them as before (immutable Pod
  fields such as the command still need a delete first; the error
  says so).
- The tool stays annotated destructive because of `replace`.

Core.PodsRun keeps its signature and behaviour (replace) for other
callers; the tool uses the new PodsRunWithOptions. The test of the
re-run now expects the refusal, and the re-apply with replace.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
